  "entry": "code/app.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load melt-curve and melt-peak text exports, pair them per well automatically, look at replicate curves and −dF/dT peaks side by side, remove outlier replicates, normalize, smooth or average the curves, and export the plots. Scope: this tree covers the Streamlit app only. The reviewer reports that the README recommends a standalone HTML version with an all-wells mean ± SD overlay, separate curve/peak Y-axis scaling and a combined long PNG. None of those were explored here. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
